, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about Napoleon in Russia."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking to Repeat"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use different phrases to ask someone to repeat something. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " <span class =\"strong\">Guide</span> : They tried to destroy the city for three days.<br /> <span class =\"strong\">Anne</span> : Say that again, please.<br /> <span class =\"strong\">Guide</span> : Three days."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Asking Someone to Repeat </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sorry?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Please speak slowly.I can't understand you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you repeat that, please?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Say that again, please.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sorry, I didn't catch that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What did you say?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slowly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not fast  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They walked very slowly. Everyone passed them. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Napoleon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a French military leader in the 1800s.  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Napoleon made the French Empire larger. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to order "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to command soldiers to do something   "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Napoleon ordered his men to destroy the Kremlin. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to blow up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to destroy by explosion "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They blew up part of the Kremlin wall."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "explosive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a material made to burst violently  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They used explosives to put a hole in the mountain. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fuse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cord to carry fire to an explosive  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He lit the fuse and we all ran behind the shelter. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fortunately "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "luckily; happily  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Fortunately, no one was hurt in the fire."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le02ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le02ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online to find out about an event in your city that happened in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 to 7 sentences about it."}, {"type": 